"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin Chrome 159's dash layout on square `dashed` / `dotted` borders:
a dash is 2t long (dotted: t), every side starts and ends on a dash, and the
gap is stretched or shrunk from t to the dash count that fits best
(StrokeData::SelectBestDashGap). A side too short for two dashes and a gap
paints solid.
Audience: browser-engine maintainers.

Chrome 159 (arm64 headless, --force-device-scale-factor=1, 160x48 and 210x70
viewports): the pins are every border-band pixel that Chrome paints as exactly
the border or background colour (1050, plus 3260 on the short-side page), plus 1x dotted pins (2px and 3px dots, below):
Partially covered dash ends and Chrome round dots (4px and wider) are not
pinned.

Thin borders (device thickness < 3) use dash 3t / gap 2t, not 2t / t; the
THIN pins below are Chrome 159 at --force-device-scale-factor=1 (1px and 2px
borders, ink is a red channel below 40, paper above 215).
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-BORDER-DASH-LAYOUT-CHROME159-001 — square dashed and dotted borders lay out their dashes as Chrome 159 does.
"""
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{simple_web_layout_render_html_software_pixels}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_renderer.{simple_web_render_html_to_pixels_with_resolved_engine2d_backend}

